  "worked_solution": "We need to create a table of values and then sketch the curve. First, we work out the $x$-values using the formula $x={t}^{2}.$ This gives\n\n| **$t$** | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $4$ | $9$ | $16$ | $25$ |\n| $y$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nNow, we work out the $y$ values using $y=t(5-t).$ This gives\n\n| **$t$** | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $4$ | $9$ | $16$ | $25$ |\n| $y$ | $0$ | $4$ | $6$ | $6$ | $4$ | $0$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nPlotting these points, we obtain the following curve:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13949104/assets/1aa848f287660c0858d5d6478da71c5baab9252c13f0a2d4a48c38d61f6bce51.png)",
